{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791297321840,"sessionID":"ses_eee5cf18cffePA3iRjCm28qvbe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"write_1_8ead0501","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/kimi-max__prose__r1__1791297260/work/rewritten.txt","content":"Last quarter, the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0. Previously, the routing table lived in several scattered files. The upgrade consolidated it into a single file at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml. The daemon reads this file once at startup and caches it in memory. The cache lasts until the process restarts or the supervisor sends a reload signal. Operators had edited the old files directly in the past. They received advice to validate every change first. Run the reload command with the --dry-run flag before any reload. A malformed entry that slips through would force every worker in the pool onto the default route. The incident review found that this fallback costs roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges. The reload command prints a diff of the routes that would change. It exits with a nonzero status if any entry fails to parse. Teams can therefore wire it into a pre-commit hook without much effort. The migration automatically converted older entries written for the previous schema. It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/kimi-max__prose__r1__1791297260/work/rewritten.txt","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/kimi-max__prose__r1__1791297260/work/rewritten.txt","time":{"start":1791297321835,"end":1791297321840}},"id":"prt_111a3e54b001c1p2taMkm8Wixk","sessionID":"ses_eee5cf18cffePA3iRjCm28qvbe","messageID":"msg_111a35033001PH2nKRaIHQsx09"}}
